/surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Dixon</surname><given-names>WT</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>MRI techniques for cardiovascular imaging</article-title><source>J Magn Reson Imaging</source><year>1999</year><volume>10</volume><fpage>590</fpage><lpage>601</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10548767</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B30"><label>30</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Reeder</surname><given-names>SB</given-names></name><name><surname>Du</surname><given-names>YP</given-names></name><name><surname>Lima</surname><given-names>JAC</given-names></name><name><surname>Bluemke</surname><given-names>DA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Advance cardiac MR imaging of ischemic heart disease</article-title><source>RadioGraphics</source><year>2001</year><volume>21</volume><fpage>1047</fpage><lpage>1074</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11452080</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B31"><label>31</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lee</surname><given-names>JJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Tirman</surname><given-names>PJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Chang</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>The optimization of scan timing for contrast-enhanced magnetic resonance angiography</article-title><source>Korean J Radiol</source><year>2000</year><volume>1</volume><fpage>142</fpage><lpage>151</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11752945</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B32"><label>32</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lee</surname><given-names>JJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Chang</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Kang</surname><given-names>D-S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Contrast-